# IBKR Gateway — Single Source of Truth

RULE: All IBKR connectivity routes through `ibkr-gateway-infra` (the long-lived IB Gateway Java process). Never reimplement IBKR auth or session management anywhere else in the workspace.
WHY: IB Gateway allows limited simultaneous connections. Duplicating auth/connection setup across UMI, execution-service, position-balance-monitor-service, instruments-service causes session conflicts and DRY violations.
CODEX: 04-architecture/TIER-ARCHITECTURE.md

DO:
 # T2 interface adapters connect to the running ibkr-gateway-infra process via ib_insync
 from ib_insync import IB
 ib = IB()
 ib.connect(host, port, clientId=client_id)  # host/port from UnifiedCloudConfig, injected by caller

NEVER:
 Spin up a new IB Gateway process per-adapter or per-service
 Hardcode IB Gateway host/port — always inject from UnifiedCloudConfig
 Use standard HTTP VCR cassettes for IBKR tests (TWS uses proprietary socket protocol, not HTTP)
  → Mock at the ib_insync object level instead (mock IB(), EClient, EWrapper)
 Add ib_insync connection logic outside of the four designated adapter files:
  unified_market_interface/adapters/ibkr_adapter.py
  unified_trade_execution_interface/adapters/ibkr_tradfi.py
  unified_position_interface/adapters/ibkr.py
  unified_reference_data_interface/adapters/ibkr.py
